<article class="env-lemma" id="0ET2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ET2">Lemma <span data-tag="0ET2">93.6.4</span>.</a> In Example <a href="/tag/0D3K" data-tag="0D3K">93.6.1</a> assume $\Gamma $ is topologically finitely generated. Let $\rho _0 : \Gamma \to \text{GL}_ k(V)$ be a finite dimensional representation. Assume $\Lambda $ is a complete local ring with residue field $k$ (the classical case). Then the functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  F : \mathcal{C}_\Lambda \longrightarrow \textit{Sets},\quad A \longmapsto \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}\! \mathit{ef}_{V, \rho _0}(A))/\cong  \]
</div>
  <p> of isomorphism classes of objects has a hull. If $H^0(\Gamma , \text{End}_ k(V)) = k$, then $F$ is prorepresentable. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The proof is exactly the same as the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0ET1" data-tag="0ET1">93.5.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>